  "design_bug": {
    "symptom": "comboPers minus comboPrior is exactly +0.0000 with a zero-width CI at every m, and the same holds for the marginal arm",
    "cause": "the personalisation arm added a SINGLE constant offset to every candidate score. Adding the same constant to all scores cannot change a ranking, so the top-k is identical to the prior by construction. The experiment could never have detected a personalisation effect.",
    "how_it_was_caught": "an exact zero with a zero-width interval is the same signature that exposed the invalid R104 run, so it was caught immediately rather than reported as a null result",
    "the_fix": "estimate per-drug residual effects from the m measured keys (as R76 did), not a single cell-level offset, so the correction actually reorders candidates"
  },
  "interesting_byproduct": {
    "combo_prior_minus_marginal_prior": "positive at all five m (+0.54 to +1.61 pp) but never significant",
    "reading": "consistent with C80: the combined prior is better than marginals by a small amount that a 30-draw design cannot resolve"
